\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The two-stock benchmark (Propositions\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {prop:benchmark} and\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {prop:floor}). (a) Corner caps, their sum and the demand floor $D=2$ as functions of the aggregate stock; the shaded band $(\genfrac  {}{}{}1{27}{5},\genfrac  {}{}{}1{69}{5})$ is the epistemic--institutional obstruction. (b) The control set $U_2$ and the cap box at $Y=6$: the box $[0,\genfrac  {}{}{}1{11}{10}]\times [0,\genfrac  {}{}{}1{39}{50}]$ lies strictly below the demand facet; the pooled row with weights $(\genfrac  {}{}{}1{1}{2},\genfrac  {}{}{}1{1}{2})$ is the line $u_1+u_2=\genfrac  {}{}{}1{47}{25}$, margin $-\genfrac  {}{}{}1{3}{50}$. (c) The demand-floor law $Y^\ast (D)=\qopname  \relax m{min}(\genfrac  {}{}{}1{77}{5}-5D,\genfrac  {}{}{}1{69}{5})$ with its physical plateau, its epistemic--institutional slope and the region without viable fibres.\relax }}{10}{figure.caption.9}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:bench}{{2}{10}{The two-stock benchmark (Propositions~\ref {prop:benchmark} and~\ref {prop:floor}). (a) Corner caps, their sum and the demand floor $D=2$ as functions of the aggregate stock; the shaded band $(\tfr {27}5,\tfr {69}5)$ is the epistemic--institutional obstruction. (b) The control set $U_2$ and the cap box at $Y=6$: the box $[0,\tfr {11}{10}]\times [0,\tfr {39}{50}]$ lies strictly below the demand facet; the pooled row with weights $(\tfr 12,\tfr 12)$ is the line $u_1+u_2=\tfr {47}{25}$, margin $-\tfr 3{50}$. (c) The demand-floor law $Y^\ast (D)=\min (\tfr {77}5-5D,\tfr {69}5)$ with its physical plateau, its epistemic--institutional slope and the region without viable fibres.\relax }{figure.caption.9}{}}
