\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces (a) Minimal infeasible subfamily sizes of random row systems with $m=k+3$ rows on $[-1,1]^k$ (Remark\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {rem:random}; $n$ is the number of infeasible systems among the draws). The size $k+1$ of Theorem\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {thm:helly} is attained but rare; with rank-one coefficients in $k=3$ the size never exceeds $2$. (b) The integrated certificate of the three-branch instance, $\Gamma _h(\tau )=\genfrac  {}{}{}1{7}{50}-\tau $ (Proposition\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {prop:integrated}), against the companion's $\Gamma (\tau )=\tau -\genfrac  {}{}{}1{7}{50}$; both cross zero at $\tau ^\ast =\genfrac  {}{}{}1{7}{50}$.\relax }}{15}{figure.caption.12}\protected@file@percent }
